    "updated_at": "2021-01-14T22:27:49Z",
    "body": "@mickimnet the default configuration *does* use conditional formatting, so it doesn't print [] if there is no status to report. What I would like is to be able to set `git_status.stash` = `false` or `''` in my config (default is `'\\$'`) and have starship expand to None rather than `'[]'` when I am in a got repo that has something stashed.\r\n\r\nI think that this logic could be applied to more things than just git_status: if we went with `''` then the rule (from the above-linked docs) would go from:\r\n\r\n    (@$region) will show nothing if the variable region is None, otherwise @ followed by the value of region.\r\n\r\nto\r\n\r\n    (@$region) will show nothing if the variable region is None or '', otherwise @ followed by the value of region.\r\n\r\nWhat would break if we did this?\r\n\r\nIf we think that nothing would break then I'm happy to submit a patch. If we think that too much would break and we have to use `false` in our toml then it would probably be a lot more work. ",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
